<Text>&lt;P style=&quot;BORDER-BOTTOM: windowtext 0.75pt solid; BORDER-LEFT: medium none; PADDING-BOTTOM: 1pt; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; PADDING-LEFT: 0in; PADDING-RIGHT: 0in; BORDER-TOP: medium none; BORDER-RIGHT: medium none; PADDING-TOP: 0in&quot; class=MsoTitle align=center&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT size=5 face=Arial&gt;DFT-S-OFDM Example&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; class=MsoNormal align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-FAMILY: Arial; FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;Keysight Technologies SystemVue Template Workspace&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;?xml:namespace prefix = o ns = &quot;urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office&quot; /&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; class=MsoNormal align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; class=MsoBodyText&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;This example is to demo to create a DFT-S-OFDM source and receiver.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;DFT-S-OFDM&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;This folder includes an example to demo DFT-S-OFDM generator. 100 mapping signals (QPSK, 16-QAM and etc) in ntime-domain&amp;nbsp;are transftered into frequency domain by DFT. These 100 frequency domain signals are loaded into a 128 point IFFT (50 signals are loaded into the positive frequency part, other 50 are loaded into minus frequency part) and&amp;nbsp;center&amp;nbsp;28 oints are filled with 0. Then, these signals (100 frequency domain siganl+zeros) are transftered into time domain by using IFFT. The mapping siganl is&amp;nbsp;interpolated after&amp;nbsp;above procedure. The constellation has four points (QPSK)&amp;nbsp;if the mapping signal is QPSK.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;DFT-S-OFDM-BER-Sim&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;This folder includes an example to demo BER of DFT-S-OFDM source and receiver. In DFT-S-OFDM source, 25 DFT-S-OFDM symbols consist of one frame, each symbol consists of 32 point cyclic prefix and 128 points IFFT. In the receiver, the basic function includes timing and frequency synchronization, channel estimation and equalizer.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;DFT-S-OFDM-BER_CS&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;This folder includes an example to demo BER of DFT-S-OFDM with Keysight instruments (MXG/PXA).&amp;nbsp; &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;</Text>
